/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Stray output from backgrounded processes (e.g. `nohup cargo run &`).
nohup.out

# Override global asdf/mise ignores -- the toolchain pin is part
# of the repo so contributors get a reproducible build.
!.tool-versions

# Per-user Claude Code overrides (destructive git ops, scratch
# Read paths, one-off Bash allows). Shared repo-wide permissions
# live in .claude/settings.json -- collaborators inherit those
# automatically; anything sensitive or personal stays in
# settings.local.json on each machine.
.claude/settings.local.json
# Per-session worktrees that Claude Code's agent system creates
# under .claude/worktrees/ for isolated sub-agent runs. They live
# only as long as the owning session and aren't part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/
# Ad-hoc tracing-log captures from `:w /tmp/...` or
# `LATTICE_STDERR=1 ... 2>logs.txt` redirects. Useful for
# interactive bug investigation; not part of the repo.
logs.txt
*.log
# Website content generated by site/scripts/sync-docs.sh from docs/{user,dev}/.
# The docs live in docs/; these are build artifacts. Tracking them meant the
# checked-in copies silently drifted (40 stale pages against 113 real ones) and,
# once topics move between sections, stale pages linger at their old URLs and
# Zola happily builds both. Run the sync before `zola build` / `zola serve`.
site/content/docs/**/*.md
!site/content/docs/_index.md
site/content/dev/**/*.md
!site/content/dev/_index.md
# The per-section `_index.md` used to be hand-authored, one per docs/dev/
# subdir. They are generated from site/data/dev-nav.toml now — title,
# description and order all come from the manifest — so they are build output
# like the user-doc section landings above, not content to edit here.
site/static/docs-search.json
site/data/version.toml

# Ad-hoc screenshots / scratch assets for bug investigation.
# Not part of the repo; lives in assets/tmp/ for ergonomic
# `Read` access during diagnosis.
assets/tmp/

# Windows "mark of the web" Alternate-Data-Stream sidecars. The colon in
# the name is an illegal path char on Windows and aborts actions/checkout.
*:Zone.Identifier

.tokensave/

# Zola build output
site/public/

# PM.2: dev runtime root — core-plugin wasm staged by `cargo xtask build-core-plugins`.
/runtime

# Test debris: `c_c_f_diff_item_actually_opens_a_diff_buffer_not_just_dismiss`
# must write inside a real git repo (the file-dispatch handler's
# `Repository::discover` needs one), so it writes here and cleans up via
# RAII. A SIGKILL'd test run skips destructors and leaves one behind —
# ignored so it can never be committed by accident.
lattice-magit-file-dispatch-test-*.txt
.gstack/
